  },
  {
    "id": "CALC1-FIN-006",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-final-2024",
    "topicId": "top-c1-deriv",
    "question": "Given that ∛(x²) + ∛(y²) = 2, then dy/dx at the point (1, 1) equals:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "0"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "2"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "-1"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "d",
    "explanation": "Differentiating implicitly: (2/3)x^(-1/3) + (2/3)y^(-1/3) * (dy/dx) = 0. At (1, 1): (2/3)(1) + (2/3)(1)(dy/dx) = 0 => dy/dx = -1.",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "sourceFile": "Final calcu 2023-2024.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 1,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "CALC1-FIN-007",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-final-2024",
    "topicId": "top-c1-curve",
    "question": "At x = 5, the function f(x) = ∛(x - 5) has:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "a vertical tangent"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "a cusp"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "a relative maximum"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "a relative minimum"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "a",
    "explanation": "f'(x) = 1 / [3(x - 5)^(2/3)]. Since the denominator is always positive and approaches 0 as x → 5 from both sides, lim_{x → 5} f'(x) = +∞, indicating a vertical tangent.",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "sourceFile": "Final calcu 2023-2024.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 1,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "CALC1-FIN-008",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-final-2024",
    "topicId": "top-c1-curve",
    "question": "The function f(x) = x(x - 4)³ is increasing on:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "(-∞, ∞)"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "(0, ∞)"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "[1, ∞)"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "(-∞, 1]"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "c",
    "explanation": "f'(x) = (x - 4)³ + 3x(x - 4)² = (x - 4)² (x - 4 + 3x) = (x - 4)² (4x - 4). Since (x - 4)² ≥ 0 everywhere, the sign depends on 4x - 4 ≥ 0, which yields x ≥ 1, so the interval is [1, ∞).",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "sourceFile": "Final calcu 2023-2024.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 1,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "CALC1-FIN-009",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-final-2024",
    "topicId": "top-c1-curve",
    "question": "The function f(x) = x |x - 2| is concave up on:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "(-∞, ∞)"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "(0, ∞)"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "(2, ∞)"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "(-∞, 2)"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "c",
    "explanation": "For x > 2, |x - 2| = x - 2, so f(x) = x² - 2x => f''(x) = 2 > 0 (concave up). For x < 2, f(x) = -x² + 2x => f''(x) = -2 < 0 (concave down). Therefore it is concave up on (2, ∞).",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "sourceFile": "Final calcu 2023-2024.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 1,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "CALC1-FIN-010",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-final-2024",
    "topicId": "top-c1-integ",
    "question": "Evaluate the indefinite integral: ∫ (1 + sin²θ csc θ) dθ =",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "θ + sin θ + c"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
