  {
    "id": "CALC1-FIN-014",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-final-2024",
    "topicId": "top-c1-integ",
    "question": "The area of the region in the first quadrant, which is bounded by the coordinate axes and the curve of the function f(x) = cos(x) is equal to:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "2 square units"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "1.5 square units"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "2.5 square units"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "1 square unit"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "d",
    "explanation": "In the first quadrant, cos(x) is bounded between x = 0 and x = π/2. Area = ∫₀^(π/2) cos(x) dx = [sin(x)]₀^(π/2) = sin(π/2) - sin(0) = 1 square unit.",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "sourceFile": "Final calcu 2023-2024.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 2,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z",
