  {
    "id": "CALC1-FIN-015",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-final-2024",
    "topicId": "top-c1-integ",
    "question": "The arc length of the curve of the function f(x) = 2√(x³) + 1 from x = 0 to x = 1 is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "(2/27)(10√10 + 1)"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "(2/27)(19√19 + 1)"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "(2/27)(10√10 - 1)"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "(2/27)(19√19 - 1)"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "c",
    "explanation": "f(x) = 2 x^(3/2) + 1 => f'(x) = 3 x^(1/2). Arc length L = ∫₀¹ √(1 + [f'(x)]²) dx = ∫₀¹ √(1 + 9x) dx = [(2/27)(1 + 9x)^(3/2)]₀¹ = (2/27)(10√10 - 1).",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "sourceFile": "Final calcu 2023-2024.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 3,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z",
