  {
    "id": "CALC1-MID-001",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-mid",
    "topicId": "top-c1-limits",
    "question": "The range of the function f(x) = 1 / √(9 - x²) is:",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "(0, 3)"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "[0, 3]"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "[1/3, ∞)"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "(1/3, ∞)"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "c",
    "explanation": "For the domain, 9 - x² > 0 => -3 < x < 3. The maximum of √(9 - x²) occurs at x = 0, giving √9 = 3. As x approaches ±3, √(9 - x²) approaches 0⁺. Thus the range is [1/3, ∞).",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "sourceFile": "ميد كالكولاس 1.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 1,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.966Z",
