        "text": "(0, (ln 2)/4)"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "(-(ln 2)/4, 0)"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "a",
    "explanation": "Divide both sides by e^(3x): e^(4x) > 2. Taking natural logarithm: 4x > ln 2 => x > (ln 2) / 4. In interval notation: ((ln 2)/4, ∞).",
    "difficulty": "Easy",
    "sourceFile": "ميد كالكولاس 1.pdf",
