  },
  {
    "id": "CALC1-MID-008",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-mid",
    "topicId": "top-c1-limits",
    "question": "Evaluate the limit: lim_{x → 3} [ 1 / (x - 3) - 27 / (x³ - 27) ] =",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "-1"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "1"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "1/3"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "-1/3"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "c",
    "explanation": "x³ - 27 = (x - 3)(x² + 3x + 9). Common denominator: [(x² + 3x + 9) - 27] / [(x - 3)(x² + 3x + 9)] = (x² + 3x - 18) / [...] = [(x - 3)(x + 6)] / [(x - 3)(x² + 3x + 9)]. Substituting x = 3: (3 + 6) / (9 + 9 + 9) = 9 / 27 = 1/3.",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "sourceFile": "ميد كالكولاس 1.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 2,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.967Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.967Z"
  },
  {
    "id": "CALC1-MID-009",
    "subjectId": "subj-calc1",
    "quizId": "quiz-calc1-mid",
    "topicId": "top-c1-limits",
    "question": "If y = 0 and x = 2 are horizontal and vertical asymptotes (respectively) of the function f(x) = [ax³ - x(3x + 1)] / [x³ - b], then a + b =",
    "options": [
      {
        "id": "a",
        "text": "3"
      },
      {
        "id": "b",
        "text": "11"
      },
      {
        "id": "c",
        "text": "8"
      },
      {
        "id": "d",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "c",
    "explanation": "For horizontal asymptote y = 0: degree of numerator must be less than denominator, so a = 0. For vertical asymptote at x = 2: x³ - b = 0 at x = 2 => 2³ - b = 0 => b = 8. Thus a + b = 0 + 8 = 8.",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "sourceFile": "ميد كالكولاس 1.pdf",
    "sourcePage": 3,
    "status": "Verified",
    "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.967Z",
    "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T16:31:10.967Z"
  },
  {
